{# The one place that says which icons turn round under a right-to-left page.

   An icon that points along the line of reading - an arrow, a chevron - has to point the other
   way once the line runs right to left. It is mirrored in place with the `rtl:-scale-x-100`
   utility rather than duplicated as a second set of SVG files. Every icon that carries no
   direction (cart, check, close, heart...) is left alone.

   The list is the theme's own icon set, named one by one rather than guessed from a `-left` or
   `-right` suffix: a suffix rule misses a directional icon named otherwise (`next`,
   `arrow-narrow-right`) and mirrors one that is not (`align-left`, `text-right`). Adding a
   directional icon to `assets/icons/` means adding its name here, and nowhere else.

   Called by the three molecules that take an icon name as a prop (Button, Link, Tabulation) and
   by every template that renders an icon itself:

       {% import '@Flexy/Atoms/Icon/direction.html.twig' as icon_direction %}
       <span class="MenuItem-icon {{ icon_direction.mirror_class('chevron-right') }}">

   A theme that inherits from Flexy inherits this file with it. #}

{% macro mirror_class(name) %}
{%- set directional = ['arrow-left', 'arrow-right', 'chevron-left', 'chevron-right'] -%}
{{- name in directional ? 'rtl:-scale-x-100' : '' -}}
{% endmacro %}
